{"key":"enterprise/T1203","id":"T1203","name":"Exploitation for Client Execution","domain":"enterprise","level":"technique","parent_id":null,"tactics":["execution"],"platforms":["Linux","macOS","Windows"],"environments":["cloud-hosted-endpoint","onprem"],"environment_basis":"project_taxonomy_from_upstream_platforms","summary":"Adversaries may exploit software vulnerabilities in client applications to execute code. Vulnerabilities can exist in software due to unsecure coding practices that can lead to unanticipated behavior. Adversaries can take advantage of certain vulnerabilities through targeted exploitation for the purpose of arbitrary code execution. Oftentimes the most valuable exploits to an offensive toolkit are those that can be used to obtain code execution…","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1203","source_stix_id":"attack-pattern--be2dcee9-a7a7-4e38-afd6-21b31ecc3d63","source_modified":"2025-10-24T17:49:18.695Z","source_object_version":"1.5","telemetry":{"status":"mapped","components":[{"id":"DC0038","name":"Application Log Content","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0038","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--9c2fa0ae-7abc-485a-97f6-699e3b6cf9fa","page":"telemetry/DC0038/"},{"id":"DC0055","name":"File Access","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0055","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--235b7491-2d2b-4617-9a52-3c0783680f71","page":"telemetry/DC0055/"},{"id":"DC0039","name":"File Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0039","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--2b3bfe19-d59a-460d-93bb-2f546adc2d2c","page":"telemetry/DC0039/"},{"id":"DC0061","name":"File Modification","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0061","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--84572de3-9583-4c73-aabd-06ea88123dd8","page":"telemetry/DC0061/"},{"id":"DC0082","name":"Network Connection Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0082","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--181a9f8c-c780-4f1f-91a8-edb770e904ba","page":"telemetry/DC0082/"},{"id":"DC0078","name":"Network Traffic Flow","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0078","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--a7f22107-02e5-4982-9067-6625d4a1765a","page":"telemetry/DC0078/"},{"id":"DC0032","name":"Process Creation","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/datacomponents/DC0032","stix_id":"x-mitre-data-component--3d20385b-24ef-40e1-9f56-f39750379077","page":"telemetry/DC0032/"}],"strategies":[{"id":"DET0287","name":"Exploitation for Client Execution – cross-platform behavior chain (browser/Office/3rd-party apps)","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0287","stix_id":"x-mitre-detection-strategy--1894c2d7-ce4f-4cfd-8644-decb1e14f0c5","relationship_id":"relationship--f094c21c-9872-4e82-88c1-c759979c4f10"}],"analytics":[{"id":"AN0797","name":"Analytic 0797","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0287#AN0797","guidance":"Cause→effect chain: (1) A client app (browser, Office, PDF/Flash/reader) experiences a crash/abnormal exit or loads from an unusual location, then (2) drops or modifies a file in user-writable paths, and/or (3) spawns an unexpected child (e.g., powershell/cmd/mshta/rundll32/wscript/installer), and (4) establishes outbound C2-like connections shortly after. Correlate application logs, file writes, process lineage, and network egress within a short window.","platforms":["Windows"],"strategy_id":"DET0287"},{"id":"AN0798","name":"Analytic 0798","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0287#AN0798","guidance":"Cause→effect chain: (1) Browser/Office/reader process logs crash/segfault or abnormal sandbox message, (2) new executable/script/write occurs in $HOME (Downloads, ~/.cache, /tmp), (3) unexpected child like curl/wget/bash/python opens network connections soon after.","platforms":["Linux"],"strategy_id":"DET0287"},{"id":"AN0799","name":"Analytic 0799","url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0287#AN0799","guidance":"Cause→effect chain: (1) App crash/abnormal termination in unified logs for Safari/Chrome/Office/Preview, (2) new files/scripts in ~/Library, ~/Downloads, /private/var/folders/*, (3) unexpected child (osascript, zsh, bash, curl) spawned by those apps, (4) new outbound connections.","platforms":["macOS"],"strategy_id":"DET0287"}],"log_sources":[{"component_id":"DC0038","component":"Application Log Content","name":"WinEventLog:Application","channel":"EventCode=1000","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN0797","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0287#AN0797","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0038/"},{"component_id":"DC0039","component":"File Creation","name":"WinEventLog:Sysmon","channel":"EventCode=11","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN0797","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0287#AN0797","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0039/"},{"component_id":"DC0032","component":"Process Creation","name":"WinEventLog:Sysmon","channel":"EventCode=1","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN0797","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0287#AN0797","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0032/"},{"component_id":"DC0082","component":"Network Connection Creation","name":"WinEventLog:Sysmon","channel":"EventCode=3, 22","platforms":["Windows"],"analytic_id":"AN0797","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0287#AN0797","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0082/"},{"component_id":"DC0038","component":"Application Log Content","name":"linux:syslog","channel":"browser/office crash, segfault, abnormal termination","platforms":["Linux"],"analytic_id":"AN0798","source_url":"https://attack.mitre.org/detectionstrategies/DET0287#AN0798","validation":"upstream_definition_not_locally_validated","component_page":"telemetry/DC0038/"},{